# MANIFEST.md5 -- the fielded static shell 0x3F1A560F (docs/FIELDED_SHELL.md).
#
# `md5sum -c MANIFEST.md5` from inside this directory. Generated 2026-09-22 from
# the ONLY complete copy on this workstation:
#   fpga/dfx/build_mint_2026_09/prod/          (gitignored: fpga/dfx/build*/)
#   fpga/dfx/build_mint_2026_09/shell_proj/    (same tree -- this mint kept the
#                                               shell project INSIDE the build
#                                               dir, unlike 0xA8C1C535's
#                                               build/shell_proj_mint/)
#
# static_routed_locked.dcp is the one that matters. Every future `make add-rm-*
# BUILD=build_mint_2026_09` reads it (fpga/dfx/build_dfx.tcl, incremental mode).
# Without it, no new overlay can ever be added to the shell that is on the board
# -- the only remedy is a full re-mint, which strands all eleven overlays already
# fielded.
#
# config_rm_greybox_fw.bit is listed here and was NOT listed for 0xA8C1C535. It
# is the exact image the config SD carries: the greybox base with this mint's
# firmware baked in by updatemem. Its firmware was built from a DIRTY tree
# (cb31b0f2 + an uncommitted DUT_EGRESS flag -- docs/FIELDED_SHELL.md says so
# plainly), so it is NOT reproducible from any commit. That is precisely why the
# bytes are worth a checksum.
#
